# Environment
#
# Match EVERY .env variant, not a hand-listed few. On 2026-09-09 a
# `.env.bak-preconsolidation` holding the Space-Track password, the
# Supabase service key and DATABASE_URL sat in the working tree
# un-ignored, because the old rules only named `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.*.local`. Any other suffix - .bak, .save, .old, an editor's
# backup - was fair game for `git add -A`. Ignore the whole family and
# re-admit only the checked-in template.
.env*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local data — never commit satellite data to git
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jp2
*.geotiff
*.SAFE/
*.db
*.csv

# ...but not reference data that belongs in the repo.
#
# The blanket *.csv above is right for scene data and exports, which are
# large and regenerable. It is wrong for the Phase 2 seed files (UCS
# Satellite Database, UNOOSA registry) - those are small, versioned
# reference data that the ingestion has to be reproducible against, and
# a blanket ignore would have swallowed them silently at import time.
!data/seed/*.csv
!data/reference/*.csv

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
